One of the features I worked on at TRACTIAN was rebuilding the app’s Overview screen from scratch.

My work covered the screen’s architecture, layout, filters and data presentation. A key part was connecting the filter controls to the information displayed, helping users narrow down large volumes of data and find what they needed.

Working on this screen meant thinking about both the interface and what happened behind it: how data reached the screen, how user selections affected the results, and how the implementation fit into the existing application.

I collaborated with design, QA and engineering teams throughout the work. That gave me a broader understanding of the decisions behind a feature, beyond the part I was implementing myself.

It’s a piece of work I’m glad to share because it brought together several areas I enjoy: building interfaces, organizing application logic and figuring out how to make complex information easier to use.


